---

<BaseLayout
  title="New Construction Prewire Guide San Antonio | KZ Audio"
  description="Free new construction prewire guide from KZ Audio & Video: a room-by-room checklist of what to wire in a San Antonio custom home before the drywall goes up."
  schema={[articleSchema, breadcrumb]}
>

  <HeroSection
    overline="Free Guide · New Construction · San Antonio"
    heading="New Construction Prewire Guide for San Antonio Custom Homes"
    subhead="What every custom home owner should wire for before the drywall goes up. From KZ Audio & Video, running low voltage in San Antonio and the Texas Hill Country since 1999."
    ctaLabel="Download the PDF"
    ctaHref={PDF_PATH}
    secondaryCta="Or call: (210) 981-4098"
    secondaryHref="tel:2109814098"
    imageSrc={HERO}
    imageAlt="Speaker wire run to an in-wall box at framing in a Stone Oak custom home theater"
    imagePosition="object-center"
    compact={true}
  />

  <TrustBar />

  <!-- Self-contained answer, written to be quoted -->
  <section class="section bg-slate-surface">
    <div class="container-main">
      <p class="overline mb-3">The Short Answer</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-6">
        What Should You Prewire in a New Custom Home?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-stone max-w-3xl leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Run the wire for everything you might want, not just what you are sure of today. A cable run costs a few dollars at rough-in, and the same run after the drywall is up can cost hundreds of dollars plus a wall repair. At minimum that means power, cable and a recessed media box behind every planned TV; in-ceiling or in-wall speaker wire for surround sound and whole-home audio; full surround and overhead Atmos runs plus two subwoofer runs in a dedicated theater; hardwired network drops in every main room and wired access point locations; camera wiring at every exterior door and the driveway; security contacts at every door and window before insulation; and conduit from the TV wall to the equipment location. Outside, plan an outlet where the landscape lighting power supply plugs in, and lay its wire before the landscaping is finished. You do not have to buy the equipment now. You just have to run the wire.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body text-stone max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-warm-white">The one rule that saves the most money:</strong> wire for where you might want it, not just where you are certain today. Pre-wire is cheap. Retrofit is expensive. When in doubt, run the wire and cap it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Room-by-room checklist -->
  <section class="section bg-charcoal">
    <div class="container-main">
      <p class="overline mb-3">Room by Room</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-12">The Prewire Checklist</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        {rooms.map(({ title, items, note }) => (
          <article class="card p-7 flex flex-col gap-4">
            <h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-h4 text-warm-white">{title}</h3>
            <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3">
              {items.map((item) => (
                <li class="flex gap-3 text-body-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">
                  <svg class="flex-shrink-0 mt-1 text-gold" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"></polyline></svg>
                  <span>{item}</span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
            {note && <p class="text-body-sm text-stone leading-relaxed italic">{note}</p>}
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Decisions -->
  <section class="section bg-slate-surface">
    <div class="container-main">
      <p class="overline mb-3">Before Rough-In</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-12">The Decisions to Make Before Rough-In</h2>
      <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        {decisions.map(({ q, a }, i) => (
          <li class="card p-7 flex gap-5">
            <span class="font-display font-bold text-gold flex-shrink-0" style="font-size:1.75rem;line-height:1;" aria-hidden="true">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-h4 text-warm-white mb-2">{q}</h3>
              <p class="text-body-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">{a}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Sort out + mistakes -->
  <section class="section bg-charcoal">
    <div class="container-main">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
        <div>
          <p class="overline mb-3">Ask Before You Start</p>
          <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-6">What to Sort Out With Your Builder</h2>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 mb-6">
            <li class="text-body text-stone leading-relaxed">Who is running the low voltage wiring, and are they an AV specialist or a general electrician?</li>
            <li class="text-body text-stone leading-relaxed">Will the AV design be coordinated with the framing and electrical schedule, or added at the end?</li>
            <li class="text-body text-stone leading-relaxed">Is there conduit planned so cables can be upgraded later without opening walls?</li>
            <li class="text-body text-stone leading-relaxed">Which rooms get wired now, and which get conduit so the option stays open later?</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-body text-stone leading-relaxed">
            An electrician is excellent at electrical. Audio and video is a different craft. The best results come from an AV specialist who works alongside your builder from the start.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="overline mb-3">Avoid These</p>
          <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-6">The Five Most Expensive Prewire Mistakes</h2>
          <ol class="flex flex-col gap-4 list-decimal pl-5">
            {mistakes.map(({ t, d }) => (
              <li class="text-body text-stone leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-warm-white">{t}</strong> {d}</li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- When to bring in AV -->
  <section class="section bg-slate-surface">
    <div class="container-main">
      <p class="overline mb-3">Timing</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-warm-white mb-6">When to Bring In Your AV Company</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-stone mb-10 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
        Getting us in before your electrical walkthrough costs you nothing extra and saves you the most money. Waiting until the end costs the most.
      </p>
      <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-6">
        {sequence.map(({ t, d }, i) => (
          <li class="card p-6 flex flex-col gap-3">
            <span class="font-display font-bold text-gold" style="font-size:1.5rem;line-height:1;" aria-hidden="true">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-warm-white">{t}</h3>
            <p class="text-body-sm text-stone leading-relaxed">{d}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a href={PDF_PATH} class="btn-primary cursor-pointer">Download the Guide (PDF)</a>
        <a href="/low-voltage-prewire-builders-san-antonio/" class="btn-ghost cursor-pointer">Low Voltage for Builders</a>
        <a href="/home-theater-guide/" class="btn-ghost cursor-pointer">Home Theater Planning Guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    heading="Get Your New Home Wired Right"
    body="KZ Audio & Video has run low voltage on custom homes across San Antonio and the Texas Hill Country for over 20 years, with our own crew from prewire to the final walkthrough. We review your plans at no charge and show you exactly what to wire for."
    ctaLabel="Book a Free Plan Review"
    ctaHref="/contact-kz-audio-video-san-antonio-tx/"
    secondaryLabel="Call (210) 981-4098"
    secondaryHref="tel:2109814098"
  />

</BaseLayout>
